hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2987","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Yahya, narrated to us Hisham, narrated to me my father, from 'Aishah (RA), who said:
""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) only descended at Al-Muhassab to make it easier for his departure. So whoever wished could descend there, and whoever wished could leave it.""

---

**CHAPTER:**"
"2988","**
Narrated to us Salam ibn Junadah, narrated to us Waki' (on the authority of) Hisham ibn Urwah, (on the authority of) his father, (on the authority of) Aisha (RA), who said:

""The descent at Al-Muhassab is not part of the Sunnah. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) only descended there so that his departure would be easier.""

Abu Bakr (RA) said: Her statement, ""It is not part of the Sunnah,"" means it is not from the Sunnah that people are required to do as he (ﷺ) did. For everything that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did—even if it was an act of permissibility (mubah)—it may be called a Sunnah, meaning that people may take it as a precedent since it is permissible, though they are not obligated to perform that act."
